<title>NETHERLANDS: VREDESTEIN IN TALKS TO BUY DUNLOP BOOTS.</title>
<headline>VREDESTEIN IN TALKS TO BUY DUNLOP BOOTS.</headline>
<dateline>AMSTERDAM 1996-09-18</dateline>
<text>
<p>Tyre-maker Vredestein NV said its Hevea unit was negotiating to buy the rubber boots business of British firm Dunlop-Slazenger.</p>
<p>Vredestein said the two companies had already reached broad agreement on the terms of the deal and expected to reach afinal agreement in about eight weeks.</p>
<p>Dunlop's rubber boots business is based in Liverpool, Engeland, and employs 90 people. Hevea, based in Raalte, employs 250 people.</p>
<p>-- Amsterdam newsroom +31 20 504 5000, Fax +31 20 504 5040</p>
